# CODEOWNERS — this repo had none, and it is the PUBLIC one.
#
# Added 2026-08-18 as the precondition for branch protection. Order matters: a
# "require Code-Owner review" rule against a repo with no owners is the
# empty-lane-team trap in reverse — the rule looks enforced and blocks nothing.
# So the owners land first, the ruleset second.
#
# WHY THIS REPO IS THE URGENT ONE. `bundle` is PUBLIC and carries the crypto
# core (DSSE signing, ML-DSA, key wrapping, the policy engine) and SPEC.md, the
# contract every other repo builds against. It also had ZERO rulesets while the
# GB10 machine account held `push` — measured 2026-08-18. All sixteen commits on
# main arrived through PRs #1-#16, so the discipline has held by convention,
# which is precisely the state that reads as enforcement right up until the day
# it doesn't.
#
# ⚠ A TEAM WITHOUT WRITE ACCESS IS SILENTLY IGNORED AS AN OWNER. Before trusting
# this file, confirm @Blak-Box/core has write on THIS repo:
#     gh api repos/Blak-Box/bundle/teams -q '.[] | "\(.slug) \(.permission)"'
# If it is absent, add it — otherwise the code-owner rule passes vacuously and
# this file is decoration.
#
# Lane note (decision 13): the contracts surface is lane:autonomous work — the
# GB10 opens the PRs. It owns no paths HERE as an owner, because the machine
# account is in no team and can never approve its own work. Humans review.

# Fallback — nothing merges wholly unreviewed.
*                       @Blak-Box/core

# ── THE CRYPTO CORE — both humans review. A silent change here is the one that
#    cannot be caught downstream: every appliance and every shipped bundle
#    verifies against exactly this code, and a weakened signature check looks
#    identical to a working one until someone forges a payload.
/sign.go                @Blak-Box/lane-product @Blak-Box/lane-knowledge
/mldsa.go               @Blak-Box/lane-product @Blak-Box/lane-knowledge
/keys.go                @Blak-Box/lane-product @Blak-Box/lane-knowledge
/keywrap.go             @Blak-Box/lane-product @Blak-Box/lane-knowledge
/policy.go              @Blak-Box/lane-product @Blak-Box/lane-knowledge

# ── THE CONTRACT ITSELF — SPEC.md is what the other repos implement against,
#    so a change here is a change to every consumer, including ones not written
#    yet (the LAN OpenAPI, the model-bundle and seed-bundle statement types).
/SPEC.md                @Blak-Box/lane-product @Blak-Box/lane-knowledge

# ── CI AND SUPPLY CHAIN — the FIPS tiering and the arm64 cross-compile are the
#    evidence behind the appliance's own claims; whoever can edit these can
#    quietly stop them running.
/.github/               @Blak-Box/lane-product @Blak-Box/lane-knowledge
/Makefile               @Blak-Box/lane-product @Blak-Box/lane-knowledge
/go.mod                 @Blak-Box/lane-product @Blak-Box/lane-knowledge
/go.sum                 @Blak-Box/lane-product @Blak-Box/lane-knowledge
